# Node Server

## Runtime

- Node 24, TypeScript, deploy on bering-dev with PM2
- Postgres for families, users, calendar connections, event cache, devices
- All routes under `/api/v1`

## Auth

- Password login → long-lived JWT (refresh optional)
- Kiosk: device registration endpoint → device-scoped token
- Never log or return Google refresh tokens in API responses

## Google Calendar

- OAuth initiated from mobile; callback handled by server
- Store refresh tokens encrypted; sync job normalizes events into cache
- Support multiple calendars per user with `nickname` and `color` fields

## API shape (initial)

- `POST /auth/login`, `POST /auth/register` (family setup)
- `GET/POST /calendars` — linked accounts, nicknames, colors
- `GET /events?from=&to=` — merged family events
- `POST /devices` — register kiosk, issue device token

## Config

- Single `.env` at **project root** (see `.env-sample`); server builds `DATABASE_URL` from `POSTGRES_*`
- Default `PORT=3847` (LAN-only, not WAN-forwarded); nginx on `smircich.ddns.net:443` proxies `/api/` to Node
